# Code Style

## No trampoline functions

A function that does nothing but call another function is a trampoline — delete it and inline
the implementation at the call site(s).

```ts
// ❌ Trampoline — resolveVelocity just calls resolveVelocityCurved
function resolveVelocityCurved(note, curved) { ... }
export function resolveVelocity(note, motif, v) {
  return resolveVelocityCurved(note, applyVelocityCurve(v, motif.curve));
}

// ✅ Implementation lives in the exported function; hot-path inlines the body
export function resolveVelocity(note, motif, v) {
  const curved = applyVelocityCurve(v, motif.curve);
  const base = note.velocity ?? curved;
  return Math.round(clamp(base * (note.velocityScale ?? 1) + (note.velocityOffset ?? 0), 1, 127));
}
// Hot path that pre-computes: inline the 3-line body directly
```

## No re-exports

Import from the defining module, not through a middleman.

```ts
// ❌ motif-authoring.ts re-exports from note-edit-schema.ts
export { NOTE_EDIT_FIELDS, type NoteEditField } from "./note-edit-schema.js";
// authoring-controller.ts imports via the middleman
import { type NoteEditField } from "../library/motif-authoring.js";

// ✅ Import from the source directly
import type { NoteEditField } from "../library/note-edit-schema.js";
```
